::ENG4_U06_L04_Q01::[MLA.ENG4.C.02] Scenario: A student team has copied paragraphs, unrelated photos, an unlabeled chart, and no clear speaker-note plan for explaining evidence about career certification access. Which option best improves digital presentation effectiveness? {
~A. Add unrelated photos so the deck looks more active.#Incorrect. Unrelated images distract from the message. Digital design should use visuals that clarify evidence, claims, or audience understanding.
=B. Replace copied paragraphs with concise bullets and speaker notes that explain the evidence.#Correct. This answer best applies the lesson skill with clear reasoning, appropriate evidence, and audience awareness.
~C. Keep source paragraphs on slides so the audience can read everything.#Incorrect. Dense paragraphs make slides hard to follow. Effective slides use concise text while the speaker explains evidence and reasoning.
~D. Use smaller font to fit more information onto each slide.#Incorrect. Reducing font size hurts readability and access. Revise by selecting key information instead of crowding the slide.
}

